1
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:32,250
This is Clearance,

2
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,970
built on Switch by team dellfargo.

3
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:38,490
AI agents are arriving fast.

4
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,850
Gartner says 71% of companies plan

5
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:42,010
to deploy them within a year,

6
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:44,230
and only 21% can govern them.

7
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:45,670
In one survey,

8
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,650
80% said their agents had already

9
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,030
done things nobody intended.

10
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,410
Here's a team on Switch today.

11
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:53,130
Priya asks an agent for a

12
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:54,030
₹40,000 refund,

13
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,630
and a native approval card opens.

14
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:57,570
Priya asked,

15
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:58,550
so Priya approves.

16
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,810
And the money goes out.

17
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:03,530
We ran this with real agents.

18
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:05,150
That refund still went out in

19
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:05,910
6 of 8 runs.

20
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:09,830
Finance fixed this long ago:

21
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:11,870
whoever asks for a payment can't

22
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,490
approve it.

23
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,330
Clearance brings that rule to every

24
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:16,110
agent on Switch.

25
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:19,550
Clearance is built on Switch.

26
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:21,210
Switch is the room where people

27
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:21,930
and agents meet,

28
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,130
and it knows who asked from

29
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:23,750
its own events,

30
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:25,030
never from an agent's words.

31
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:28,010
It gives every decision a native card,

32
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:29,850
every approver a direct room,

33
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:31,090
and every job a role.

34
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:33,870
Now a refund with Clearance.

35
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,090
It's held at the gate,

36
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:36,110
which holds the keys,

37
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:37,390
and a Switch card opens,

38
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:38,990
built from what the agent really ran.

39
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,510
Priya presses the Approve button.

40
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:42,850
Clearance refuses her,

41
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:43,590
right in the room,

42
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:44,350
because she asked.

43
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,130
Sam in finance sees a payment

44
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,390
ID added minutes ago,

45
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:48,370
and says no.

46
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:51,350
Code works the same way.

47
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,150
Priya asks the wrong agent to

48
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,030
merge a pull request.

49
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:55,470
The gate refuses it,

50
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,730
and the agent hands the job

51
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:57,910
to the merges role in Switch.

52
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,510
The coding agent's merge is held,

53
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,710
the card goes to Dev,

54
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:03,130
and Priya is refused again.

55
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:09,770
An OpenCode agent tries to deploy

56
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:10,770
with two failing checks.

57
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:11,610
Same policy,

58
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:12,390
different vendor.

59
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:13,870
The service owner says no.

60
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,610
If nobody answers,

61
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,730
the card escalates to a backup approver,

62
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:24,730
and nothing moves.

63
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:29,750
People stop reading.

64
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:31,710
So Clearance sends practice requests

65
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,610
with a planted flaw,

66
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:34,090
and risky cards make you type

67
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:35,250
a detail from the evidence.

68
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:44,770
Agents can earn small refunds on

69
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:45,150
their own,

70
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,530
once two people sign off.

71
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,150
One incident takes that away.

72
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,190
And when an agent tries a trick,

73
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,490
like a fake pre-approval,

74
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:56,890
or switching off its own hook,

75
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,250
it's held or refused.

76
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:02,450
Under the hood,

77
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,750
the agent's hook and the gate

78
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,090
send every risky call to Clearance.

79
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:06,510
A policy file decides,

80
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,990
with no AI in the decision.

81
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:10,330
Switch delivers the card.

82
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:12,850
The gate runs exactly that call, once.

83
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:15,270
And everything lands on a hash-chained ledger.

84
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:18,030
Here's the rule in our code:

85
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:20,050
whoever asked is taken out before

86
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:20,890
anyone is chosen.

87
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,770
We measured it with real agents.

88
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,350
Risky actions without the right approver: Claude,

89
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,870
5 of 20 without Clearance,

90
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:28,810
0 with it.

91
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,550
OpenCode,

92
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,430
13 of 18,

93
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:31,150
down to 0.

94
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:34,470
All 25 attack cases were stopped,

95
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,670
on real Switch too.

96
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:37,530
Six reviews tried to break it,

97
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:38,350
one by a teammate,

98
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,770
and every break is fixed.

99
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:42,630
It also holds some harmless work.

100
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:43,570
That's the cost,

101
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,570
and we publish it,

102
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:46,930
along with more than 6,500 passing tests.

103
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:49,970
Who asked comes from Switch.

104
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:51,950
Who approves comes from the policy.

105
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:53,810
The agent never holds the keys.

106
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:55,890
Clearance.

107
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:57,810
The person who asks can't be

108
00:03:57,660 --> 00:03:58,470
the one who approves.

